1
00:00:12,958 --> 00:00:14,125
(Ryu Se-il)

2
00:00:20,333 --> 00:00:22,042
(Ha Jung-hoon)

3
00:00:27,792 --> 00:00:29,417
(Lee Jung-chan)

4
00:00:34,875 --> 00:00:36,625
(Jung Si-wan)

5
00:00:44,917 --> 00:00:46,708
"Boy, with Caution"

6
00:01:29,375 --> 00:01:31,895
(Start a new chat with "Regret"?)
I want you to be the one, sir.

7
00:01:37,375 --> 00:01:38,750
Counsel me.

8
00:01:47,250 --> 00:01:51,292
"Boy, with Caution"
(Episode 3)

9
00:01:51,417 --> 00:01:55,000
I'd like to hear more
of your story, Mr. Regret.

10
00:02:25,750 --> 00:02:27,292
I'm pretty boring...

11
00:02:29,250 --> 00:02:31,667
Then what kind of person are you?

12
00:02:34,375 --> 00:02:36,083
Because you look like you have nothing.

13
00:02:36,833 --> 00:02:38,473
Those are the only students I look after.

14
00:02:39,708 --> 00:02:41,167
Kids like you.

15
00:02:48,958 --> 00:02:50,268
(Then what kind of person are you?)

16
00:02:50,292 --> 00:02:52,083
Someone with nothing to lose.

17
00:02:57,625 --> 00:03:00,333
If we can't get stash from Lee Hyeon-jae,

18
00:03:00,458 --> 00:03:02,125
doesn't that put us out of business?

19
00:03:02,625 --> 00:03:04,333
We don't need Lee Hyeon-jae anymore.

20
00:03:04,458 --> 00:03:08,208
There's an older guy named Ji Tae-hyeong.
He got expelled two years ago.

21
00:03:08,333 --> 00:03:11,583
He's got tons of connections.
He can get any pill you want.

22
00:03:12,125 --> 00:03:14,375
Isn't that guy fucking terrifying?

23
00:03:14,500 --> 00:03:16,125
I heard he killed someone.

24
00:03:16,250 --> 00:03:17,333
You actually believe that?

25
00:03:17,458 --> 00:03:18,500
Huh?

26
00:03:24,750 --> 00:03:26,958
That new substitute teacher...

27
00:03:27,792 --> 00:03:30,167
He's always fucking
covering for Lee Hyeon-jae.

28
00:03:30,292 --> 00:03:32,851
He's completely clueless.
No wonder he's still a temp at his age.

29
00:03:32,875 --> 00:03:33,917
Tell me about it.

30
00:03:34,042 --> 00:03:35,976
That fucking smug look
on his face pisses me off.

31
00:03:36,000 --> 00:03:38,434
Once Hyeon-jae confesses, I'm
sending him to the disciplinary committee.

32
00:03:38,458 --> 00:03:40,917
And what if he doesn't?

33
00:03:41,042 --> 00:03:42,583
Damn it, that bastard Jang Gi-woo.

34
00:03:44,500 --> 00:03:45,500
What the hell?

35
00:03:45,542 --> 00:03:46,792
Who the hell did that?

36
00:03:49,375 --> 00:03:50,750
Isn't this your phone?

37
00:03:50,875 --> 00:03:51,958
What?

38
00:03:53,333 --> 00:03:54,500
Ah, fuck!

39
00:03:56,125 --> 00:03:57,417
I missed.

40
00:03:58,625 --> 00:03:59,958
It's completely smashed.

41
00:04:01,292 --> 00:04:02,500
Here.

42
00:04:02,625 --> 00:04:04,458
Fuck, you did that on purpose, didn't you?

43
00:04:05,333 --> 00:04:06,458
Yeah.

44
00:04:07,542 --> 00:04:08,875
Give me your account number.

45
00:04:10,417 --> 00:04:11,708
What are you doing?

46
00:04:12,208 --> 00:04:13,500
Are you out of your mind?

47
00:04:13,625 --> 00:04:15,305
Didn't you want me to take responsibility?

48
00:04:15,958 --> 00:04:17,250
For stealing the phone.

49
00:04:21,667 --> 00:04:24,083
Say Jang Gi-woo's name one more time.

50
00:04:25,000 --> 00:04:26,917
If you really want to
see how crazy I can get.

51
00:04:28,417 --> 00:04:29,625
And another thing.

52
00:04:30,792 --> 00:04:33,552
If you want to keep dealing pills,
I suggest you kick the habit first.

53
00:04:35,125 --> 00:04:36,885
Seems to me the cash
blinded you completely.

54
00:04:53,250 --> 00:04:54,375
Kim Jeong-ha!

55
00:04:55,250 --> 00:04:56,583
Where is that punk Kim Jeong-ha?

56
00:04:59,833 --> 00:05:01,433
Damn it! Where the hell is Kim Jeong-ha?

57
00:05:06,167 --> 00:05:07,167
Hey.

58
00:05:07,250 --> 00:05:08,833
Where the hell is Kim Jeong-ha?

59
00:05:08,958 --> 00:05:10,167
You're making too much noise.

60
00:05:10,292 --> 00:05:11,412
Why are you looking for him?

61
00:05:11,458 --> 00:05:12,708
What's it to you?

62
00:05:12,833 --> 00:05:15,208
Then stop making a scene.

63
00:05:17,000 --> 00:05:18,333
And what if I don't?

64
00:05:28,833 --> 00:05:30,167
Was it you?

65
00:05:37,083 --> 00:05:38,583
Let's talk.

66
00:05:42,458 --> 00:05:44,250
I've got nothing to say to you.

67
00:05:44,375 --> 00:05:46,292
What the fuck is your problem?

68
00:05:47,500 --> 00:05:49,542
Hey! I paid you to do a job.

69
00:05:49,667 --> 00:05:51,458
You take the deposit
and now you're bailing?

70
00:05:52,333 --> 00:05:54,684
I paid, so aren't you supposed
to give me what I paid for?!

71
00:05:54,708 --> 00:05:56,000
Just like a vending machine!

72
00:06:05,417 --> 00:06:06,667
Kim Jeong-ha.

73
00:06:10,792 --> 00:06:12,125
Where are you going?

74
00:06:22,958 --> 00:06:23,958
The hospital?

75
00:06:24,042 --> 00:06:26,083
My grandma has no one else to care for her.

76
00:06:31,292 --> 00:06:31,917
Where's your phone?

77
00:06:32,042 --> 00:06:33,458
I'll turn it in next time.

78
00:06:34,500 --> 00:06:35,708
Hand it over.

79
00:06:48,208 --> 00:06:50,917
Here's my number. Call
me if anything happens.

80
00:06:54,417 --> 00:06:55,792
Nothing's going to happen.

81
00:06:55,917 --> 00:06:59,292
Everything you just told me
sounds like a big deal.

82
00:06:59,583 --> 00:07:03,833
So if there's any trouble, call me.

83
00:07:13,417 --> 00:07:15,167
People might get the wrong idea.

84
00:07:17,417 --> 00:07:19,792
Don't get too invested in your students.

85
00:07:20,750 --> 00:07:22,375
They might read too much into it.

86
00:07:25,542 --> 00:07:27,833
Especially the kids who are always lonely.

87
00:07:30,500 --> 00:07:32,625
Should we start talking about you first?

88
00:07:33,167 --> 00:07:36,042
I heard you studied abroad for two years.
How was it?

89
00:07:37,292 --> 00:07:38,792
I never studied abroad.

90
00:07:41,625 --> 00:07:42,833
I see.

91
00:07:43,500 --> 00:07:45,140
Then what were you doing those two years?

92
00:07:47,167 --> 00:07:48,247
A little bit of everything.

93
00:07:50,417 --> 00:07:53,167
What's been bothering you the most lately?
Tell me.

94
00:07:58,292 --> 00:08:00,083
Why did you do that
with Young-moon's phone?

95
00:08:00,208 --> 00:08:01,667
I just wanted to pay him back.

96
00:08:02,708 --> 00:08:04,500
Is the counseling session over?

97
00:08:15,917 --> 00:08:17,837
(Regret: Message)
Have you ever misinterpreted...

98
00:08:18,042 --> 00:08:19,750
someone's kindness?

99
00:08:28,917 --> 00:08:30,208
Yeah.

100
00:08:33,708 --> 00:08:35,625
I think I'm going through that...

101
00:08:38,792 --> 00:08:40,125
right now.

102
00:08:45,250 --> 00:08:46,583
Done already?

103
00:08:46,708 --> 00:08:48,417
Didn't I say I wanted to talk to you, sir?

104
00:08:48,542 --> 00:08:50,851
There's a professional counselor.
Why does it have to be me?

105
00:08:50,875 --> 00:08:54,708
If it's not you,
I don't want counseling at all.

106
00:08:56,667 --> 00:09:00,125
So you only agreed to
counseling because of me?

107
00:09:02,333 --> 00:09:03,625
Is that so wrong?

108
00:09:06,500 --> 00:09:07,708
Yes, it is.

109
00:09:09,042 --> 00:09:10,250
Why?

110
00:09:12,083 --> 00:09:13,483
Because it puts me in a tough spot.

111
00:09:16,000 --> 00:09:19,375
I won't give you a demerit for what
happened with Choi Young-moon.

112
00:09:19,500 --> 00:09:20,934
Just take your counseling
sessions seriously starting next week.

113
00:09:20,958 --> 00:09:21,958
And if I don't want to?

114
00:09:24,625 --> 00:09:26,458
If you don't...

115
00:09:27,333 --> 00:09:28,708
then forget it.

116
00:09:29,833 --> 00:09:31,042
See you tomorrow.

117
00:09:41,583 --> 00:09:43,943
It's the first time anyone's
ever cared about me like this.

118
00:09:54,833 --> 00:09:56,667
Didn't you say it was your first time?

119
00:09:57,625 --> 00:09:59,792
Then how do you know it's caring?

120
00:10:05,917 --> 00:10:07,875
Because that's how it feels.

121
00:10:17,250 --> 00:10:20,250
You're the type who
leads people on, aren't you?

122
00:10:28,958 --> 00:10:31,038
I don't think I've ever given
anyone the wrong idea.

123
00:10:31,083 --> 00:10:33,003
Give me another pack
of Terra Bold [cigarettes].

124
00:10:39,792 --> 00:10:41,625
What do you think affection is?

125
00:10:43,583 --> 00:10:45,125
When do you ever feel that way?

126
00:10:48,167 --> 00:10:49,750
I don't know.

127
00:10:49,875 --> 00:10:51,417
It's been too long.

128
00:10:53,833 --> 00:10:55,083
Are you married?

129
00:10:56,375 --> 00:10:57,917
Yes.

130
00:10:58,042 --> 00:10:59,542
Got married pretty young.

131
00:11:12,167 --> 00:11:16,458
Yet... you don't even
know what affection is?

132
00:11:19,958 --> 00:11:24,417
I don't know what I gave my wife.

133
00:11:32,500 --> 00:11:34,417
Whether it was affection or love.

134
00:11:42,667 --> 00:11:45,500
Either way, it must've been pretty dull.

135
00:11:45,625 --> 00:11:47,385
Because that's just
the kind of person I am.

136
00:11:58,333 --> 00:12:00,875
Because I liked my wife more.

137
00:12:03,417 --> 00:12:05,485
("I liked my wife more...
Wife... Wedding ring...?")

138
00:12:05,509 --> 00:12:07,217
Now, how should we
look at labeling theory?

139
00:12:08,125 --> 00:12:09,417
All right.

140
00:12:09,542 --> 00:12:10,833
Let me give you an example.

141
00:12:11,917 --> 00:12:14,208
Suppose someone goes to prison for theft.

142
00:12:25,167 --> 00:12:28,500
Deviance isn't inherent to the act itself.

143
00:12:28,625 --> 00:12:31,333
It depends on how others
react to that behavior.

144
00:12:31,458 --> 00:12:34,417
In other words, the
label people attach to it.

145
00:12:35,208 --> 00:12:37,125
That's the micro-level perspective.

146
00:12:39,417 --> 00:12:40,542
Quiet down!

147
00:12:41,458 --> 00:12:43,417
Great job at the
tournament today, everyone.

148
00:12:43,542 --> 00:12:45,875
Next time, don't just work hard.

149
00:12:46,000 --> 00:12:48,500
Bring home some results, got it?

150
00:12:48,625 --> 00:12:49,125
Yes, Coach...

151
00:12:49,250 --> 00:12:50,770
All right, let's hear it for Ho-young!

152
00:12:55,125 --> 00:12:56,458
Thanks to your bronze medal,

153
00:12:56,583 --> 00:12:58,875
we barely saved face. Good job!

154
00:12:59,000 --> 00:13:03,042
Next time, bring home at least a silver
and make our school proud, all right?

155
00:13:03,167 --> 00:13:04,375
Yes, Coach.

156
00:13:05,583 --> 00:13:09,500
No practice tomorrow or the day after.

157
00:13:11,750 --> 00:13:14,430
Everyone meet at Flame BBQ
by the three-way intersection. Dismissed!

158
00:13:19,625 --> 00:13:21,000
What are you doing here?

159
00:13:29,542 --> 00:13:30,662
Haven't eaten yet, have you?

160
00:13:36,333 --> 00:13:40,000
Your wrist is in a cast.
Must be a pretty bad injury, huh?

161
00:13:40,958 --> 00:13:43,667
The doctor said I'll be
fine after a week of rest.

162
00:13:45,708 --> 00:13:46,833
Seriously.

163
00:13:47,917 --> 00:13:48,958
Jeong-ha.

164
00:13:49,667 --> 00:13:53,792
If you want to earn a living with
your body, there are other jobs.

165
00:13:54,292 --> 00:13:57,208
You could work at a café
or a fried chicken place.

166
00:13:57,333 --> 00:13:58,833
Just like any other kid your age.

167
00:13:58,958 --> 00:14:00,000
You understand?

168
00:14:06,500 --> 00:14:08,167
I train because I truly love it.

169
00:14:09,750 --> 00:14:11,583
My life is already awful enough.

170
00:14:14,292 --> 00:14:16,417
This is the only thing that makes me happy.

171
00:14:19,083 --> 00:14:21,542
I'll rest for a week, heal
up, and come right back.

172
00:14:21,667 --> 00:14:23,000
Please...

173
00:14:24,625 --> 00:14:26,458
Can't you give me one more chance?

174
00:14:33,625 --> 00:14:34,917
Eat up.

175
00:14:37,667 --> 00:14:39,333
Let today be your last day.

176
00:14:52,500 --> 00:14:53,518
What's the deal with Kim Jeong-ha?

177
00:14:53,542 --> 00:14:54,708
Is his wrist completely shot?

178
00:14:54,833 --> 00:14:56,417
You're the one who's useless!

179
00:14:56,542 --> 00:14:57,625
You looking to get beat up?

180
00:15:09,292 --> 00:15:11,667
Have you ever met someone through this?

181
00:15:14,708 --> 00:15:15,875
Once.

182
00:15:16,500 --> 00:15:18,833
The moment they saw I was a guy, they ran.

183
00:15:19,750 --> 00:15:21,000
(I'm a guy too. Would you run?)

184
00:15:21,125 --> 00:15:22,458
I'm a guy too.

185
00:15:22,583 --> 00:15:23,958
Would you run?

186
00:15:39,792 --> 00:15:41,208
Here for lunch?

187
00:15:42,667 --> 00:15:43,750
Yes.

188
00:15:46,708 --> 00:15:48,188
Want me to treat you to some ramyeon?

189
00:15:48,875 --> 00:15:49,875
No, thanks.

190
00:16:08,542 --> 00:16:10,342
I actually feel more
comfortable around guys.

191
00:17:18,750 --> 00:17:19,917
Mr. Jang.

192
00:17:20,833 --> 00:17:22,917
You're heading back
to the office too, right?

193
00:17:23,292 --> 00:17:24,292
Let's walk together.

194
00:17:34,500 --> 00:17:36,458
Didn't I tell you?

195
00:17:40,208 --> 00:17:41,888
Leave Hyeon-jae alone as much as possible.

196
00:17:46,625 --> 00:17:48,958
Don't worry about
whether he fits in or not.

197
00:17:49,083 --> 00:17:50,792
Don't mind him.

198
00:17:53,750 --> 00:17:57,792
You keep telling me to stay out of it. Why?

199
00:18:00,208 --> 00:18:02,417
Whatever you're doing right now...

200
00:18:02,542 --> 00:18:04,083
stop doing all of it.

201
00:18:08,750 --> 00:18:10,083
May I...

202
00:18:11,000 --> 00:18:13,292
know why?

203
00:18:18,042 --> 00:18:19,333
Sir.

204
00:18:20,792 --> 00:18:22,833
Didn't something happen to you in the past?

205
00:18:25,250 --> 00:18:26,542
Am I wrong?

206
00:18:30,833 --> 00:18:33,417
Guess we've gotta get
that 500,000 won back.

207
00:18:33,542 --> 00:18:34,875
Yeah, we already paid him.

208
00:18:36,292 --> 00:18:37,833
Finish what you started yesterday.

209
00:18:40,500 --> 00:18:41,893
You acted like you were
bailing. Scared the crap out of me.

210
00:18:41,917 --> 00:18:43,083
Jeong-ha.

211
00:18:43,208 --> 00:18:44,643
I was worried you'd give the money back.

212
00:18:44,667 --> 00:18:47,250
You can pay the rest today, right?

213
00:18:48,375 --> 00:18:49,958
You must really be desperate for cash.

214
00:18:50,083 --> 00:18:52,059
Just take good photos as
proof and send them over,

215
00:18:52,083 --> 00:18:53,963
and the money will hit
your account right away.

216
00:19:07,833 --> 00:19:09,233
Come over to my place after school.

217
00:19:09,917 --> 00:19:11,333
My dad's on a business trip today.

218
00:19:11,458 --> 00:19:13,417
Don't you hate eating dinner alone?

219
00:19:13,667 --> 00:19:15,083
I can't go.

220
00:19:16,708 --> 00:19:17,708
Why?

221
00:19:19,125 --> 00:19:20,792
I asked you why.

222
00:19:21,583 --> 00:19:22,792
I have a part-time job.

223
00:19:23,500 --> 00:19:24,917
Didn't you say you quit?

224
00:19:27,500 --> 00:19:30,208
Didn't we agree last time was the last?

225
00:19:30,333 --> 00:19:32,208
A promise is a promise. Don't back out.

226
00:19:32,333 --> 00:19:32,875
And what if I do?

227
00:19:33,000 --> 00:19:34,208
Hey!

228
00:19:34,833 --> 00:19:37,792
I have things that matter
way more than a promise to you.

229
00:19:39,542 --> 00:19:41,342
Don't you have things
more important than me?

230
00:19:42,292 --> 00:19:43,452
You need to get into college.

231
00:19:45,833 --> 00:19:48,458
What if hanging around
me ruins your reputation?

232
00:19:48,583 --> 00:19:49,375
Reputation?

233
00:19:49,500 --> 00:19:50,875
Just act the way you normally do.

234
00:20:15,250 --> 00:20:16,583
This is my seat.

235
00:20:24,792 --> 00:20:25,833
I know.

236
00:20:28,125 --> 00:20:29,417
I was waiting for you.

237
00:20:40,875 --> 00:20:41,875
Hyung.

238
00:20:42,000 --> 00:20:43,292
I'm sorry.

239
00:21:05,833 --> 00:21:07,593
Guess you'll have to
use your feet now, huh?

240
00:21:30,792 --> 00:21:31,792
(Kim Jeong-ha)

241
00:21:32,250 --> 00:21:33,417
Kim Jeong-ha.

242
00:21:34,042 --> 00:21:35,250
You know me?

243
00:21:36,167 --> 00:21:37,792
Choi Young-moon sent you, didn't he?

244
00:21:52,917 --> 00:21:54,125
(Incoming Call: Jang Gi-woo)

245
00:22:05,958 --> 00:22:08,083
Hey!

246
00:22:10,375 --> 00:22:11,667
Look at me.

247
00:22:12,625 --> 00:22:13,875
Hit me.

248
00:22:18,542 --> 00:22:19,708
I said hit me.

249
00:22:20,167 --> 00:22:21,333
Go on, hit me.

250
00:22:34,125 --> 00:22:35,375
Hit me like you mean it.

251
00:22:37,125 --> 00:22:38,250
Thank you.

252
00:22:39,042 --> 00:22:42,083
There probably isn't much to
see in these counseling notes.

253
00:22:42,208 --> 00:22:44,042
Hyeon-jae had zero desire to do counseling.

254
00:22:46,542 --> 00:22:48,942
Thank you for your effort. I'll
read through them carefully.

255
00:22:51,500 --> 00:22:53,667
There's only one semester left anyway.

256
00:22:54,958 --> 00:22:58,042
And there are so many other
students who need your care.

257
00:22:58,750 --> 00:23:02,083
Honestly, Hyeon-jae doesn't
really need counseling.

258
00:23:08,625 --> 00:23:10,417
Let me know once you've thought it over.

259
00:23:21,250 --> 00:23:22,500
Sir.

260
00:23:24,917 --> 00:23:26,583
Put some meds on this for me.

261
00:23:38,500 --> 00:23:39,740
Get an excuse note and go home.

262
00:23:42,042 --> 00:23:43,125
I don't want to go home.

263
00:23:43,250 --> 00:23:44,500
After school...

264
00:23:47,542 --> 00:23:50,833
Even if you don't want to go home,
don't wander around the streets. Try to...

265
00:23:56,875 --> 00:23:58,750
I'll excuse you for today.

266
00:23:59,833 --> 00:24:01,000
Sir.

267
00:24:07,208 --> 00:24:08,958
You still give me special treatment,

268
00:24:10,333 --> 00:24:11,708
don't you?

269
00:24:22,625 --> 00:24:29,208
- Let go.
- This is the first time anyone's ever treated me special.

270
00:24:31,458 --> 00:24:33,167
You're special to me too, sir.

271
00:24:33,292 --> 00:24:37,167
So please keep treating me like this.

272
00:24:47,625 --> 00:24:49,208
Boy, with Caution.

273
00:24:49,958 --> 00:24:51,268
(Next Episode Preview)
Is this how you do things?

274
00:24:51,292 --> 00:24:53,625
Acting out like this just for attention?

275
00:24:53,750 --> 00:24:54,750
Don't ever drift apart.

276
00:24:54,875 --> 00:24:58,708
If people find out, they'll think
there's something wrong with you.

277
00:24:58,833 --> 00:25:01,333
How much longer do I
have to keep doing this?

278
00:25:01,458 --> 00:25:02,333
I'm on my way.

279
00:25:02,458 --> 00:25:03,333
Where is it?

280
00:25:03,458 --> 00:25:04,893
(Transaction Failed: Insufficient Funds)
I'll set it up for you.

281
00:25:04,917 --> 00:25:05,417
Go check it out.

282
00:25:05,542 --> 00:25:08,292
That guy... he has a thing for your type.

283
00:25:09,500 --> 00:25:12,542
If you've got no collateral, do you
want to put your body on the line?

284
00:25:12,667 --> 00:25:13,833
You have a visitor.

285
00:25:15,250 --> 00:25:16,333
A student?

286
00:25:16,458 --> 00:25:18,917
What number am I to you, sir?

287
00:25:19,958 --> 00:25:21,000
As for me...

288
00:25:21,125 --> 00:25:23,792
I want to be the only one in your heart.
